                <pb facs="0166" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/250: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sydney</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sydney</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1937-12-17T07:30:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1937-12-10T00:00:00+10:00">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        December 17, 1937—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Moore of Customs Department telephoned me today from Melbourne and asked that I
                    meet him in Canberra on Monday in order that he may go over in some detail the
                    position in which the Government finds itself in the light of present trade
                    policy. I told him I would call on him in Canberra on Monday morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
